  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Ordinal numbers",
     "texto": [
      "Up to ten they have their own forms: **der erste** (first), **der zweite** (second), **der dritte** (third), **der vierte** (fourth)… From 20 onwards **-ste** is added: **der zwanzigste** (twentieth).",
      "They are declined like an adjective in front of the noun or after «am»: **am dritten Oktober** (the 3rd of October)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Dates",
     "texto": [
      "In German the date uses the ordinal: **Heute ist der dreizehnte Oktober** (today is the 13th of October). To ask the date: **Der Wievielte ist heute?** (what's the date today?).",
      "To say «the day of the month» with «am»: **am zwanzigsten Oktober** (the 20th of October). Written with figures, a full stop is added: 20. Oktober."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
